{"parentUuid":"482e6c04-f9bf-4f76-9b54-919b72afbadc","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3b2b61ed-e095-4c38-a4b5-8f36ee037552","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Compaction Summary\n\n  1. Task Overview\n\n  User reported entire migrate --checkpoints v2 taking 20-30min for 4k checkpoints, slowdown traced to recent generation-logic patches. They asked whether entire doctor trace could diagnose,\n  or if a --verbose flag was needed. Goal: identify the actual bottleneck.\n\n  2. Current State\n\n  Implemented entire migrate --checkpoints v2 --profile (this branch: v2-migration-performance, no commits yet):\n  - New file: cmd/entire/cli/migrate_profile.go — migrateProfiler with phases (one-shot timings) + aggregated stages (count/total/avg/max), context plumbing\n  (profileStartPhase/profileStartStage), formatProfileDuration helper.\n  - New file: cmd/entire/cli/migrate_profile_test.go — unit tests for profiler + integration test (TestMigrateCheckpointsV2_ProfilerCapturesPhasesAndStages) confirming spans fire in the real\n  migration code path.\n  - Modified cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go — added --profile flag + instrumentation:\n    - Phases: list_v1_checkpoints, build_full_artifacts_index, process_checkpoints, pack_partial_generation, repair_generation_metadata\n    - Stages (per-checkpoint, aggregated): read_v2_existing, resume_packing, backfill_compact_transcripts, read_v1_summary, read_v1_session, compact_transcript, write_v2_session,\n  collect_task_metadata, pack_full_generation\n  - Lint clean, all migrate/profile tests pass.\n\n  Diagnostic findings from real-repo runs:\n\n  ┌───────────────────────────────┬────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │           Run type            │ Total  │                                        Dominant cost                                         │\n  ├───────────────────────────────┼────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n  │ Rerun (5110 ckpts, 30 fresh)  │ 13m48s │ repair_generation_metadata: 13m39s (99%)                                                     │\n  ├───────────────────────────────┼────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n  │ Fresh (2478 ckpts, all fresh) │ 5m38s  │ compact_transcript 2m + pack_full_generation 2m + write_v2_session 51s + read_v1_session 40s │\n  └───────────────────────────────┴────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n  3. Important Discoveries\n\n  - Original 20-30min reports were rerun-dominated by the repair pass, not the migration loop itself. Fresh runs scale to ~9min for 4k checkpoints.\n  - Why repair fires on near-no-op reruns: 30 freshly-migrated checkpoints land in pendingFull, the partial-generation pack at end of run trips RotateCurrentGenerationIfNeeded, which appends\n  one new archived ref to freshlyPackedRefs. That single ref trips the gate at migrate.go:172 (len(freshlyPackedRefs) > 0) — repair then walks every other archived generation (~3.4 min/archive\n   × ~4 archives = ~13.6min), even though those pre-existing archives are unchanged from prior runs.\n  - Design pivot mid-task: initially proposed using perf.Span/LoopSpan everywhere, but LoopSpan (manual_commit_hooks.go:990) emits one iteration span per pass — at 4k+ iterations × 6 sub-spans\n   each, that's 24k+ attrs in a single perf log line. Switched to a custom aggregator for per-checkpoint stages while keeping perf.Span-style timing for one-shot phases. (perf package itself\n  is untouched.)\n  - Minor reporting quirk: process_checkpoints phase wraps the entire migrateCheckpointsV2 call, so it nests the inner phases (list_v1_checkpoints, build_full_artifacts_index,\n  pack_partial_generation). Subtract those for the loop-body-only number. Fixable but not blocking.\n  - Pre-existing flake: TestResolveAgentForRewind in cmd/entire/cli/strategy/ is flaky on main too (~50% fail rate when run with the rest of the strategy suite, passes in isolation). Unrelated\n   to this work.\n\n  4. Next Steps\n\n  Recommended priority: fix the rerun blowup (bigger user-facing win, smaller blast radius). Two reasonable approaches discussed but not yet decided:\n  1. Version-tag generation.json — add e.g. \"packer_version\": \"...\" so the repair pass can skip archives already produced by the current packer. After one repair per archive, future runs are\n  O(0).\n  2. Tighten the gate at migrate.go:172 — only run repair against archives lacking the marker.\n\n  Lower priority: investigate fresh-run hot path (compact_transcript 35% + pack_full_generation 35%) for sub-stage profiling, but ~9min for 4k is tolerable.\n\n  Branch state: v2-migration-performance with uncommitted instrumentation changes. Not yet committed/pushed — user hasn't asked.\n\n  5. Context to Preserve\n\n  - User: nina@entire.io, working on Entire CLI repo at /Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli, Go 1.26.x, mise toolchain.\n  - User saved memory: don't run state-mutating commands against other repos in ~/entire/devenv/ without explicit go-ahead (e.g., no entire migrate against entire.io repo unless asked).\n  - Coding style preferences from CLAUDE.md: terse, no unnecessary comments, no over-engineering, don't add features beyond task. User confirmed terse is good (\"Perfect\", \"Perfect yeah\"\n  through this session — keep that pace).\n  - Methodology: TDD (tests first, watched RED, then GREEN), mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test:ci before commits.\n  - The --profile flag is currently hidden under entire migrate (whose parent command is Hidden: true). Likely fine to leave hidden alongside the rest of migrate.\n  - Running entire migrate --profile against a real repo requires either (a) acceptance that reruns will modify local v2 refs, or (b) the throwaway-clone recipe documented earlier in the\n  conversation (git clone --no-local …).\n\n  ---\n  The user's last meaningful question was: \"Which do you want to tackle? My vote is the rerun fix — bigger ROI, smaller blast radius.\" They never answered which path (gate-tightening vs.\n  version-tagging) — but they didn't push back on tackling the rerun fix either. Awaiting their direction."},"uuid":"16c5ea41-9bcf-4cb8-8b79-c0e54b5612cd","timestamp":"2026-05-07T18:51:32.138Z","permissionMode":"default","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"2258e038-9f02-499e-98ec-73c37394ea23","version":"2.1.132","gitBranch":"migration-performance-improvements"}
