{"parentUuid":"cd3f51d4-53df-4341-a173-14e20b99aeb9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01YCcyiWhRtoAbkWry8WGVib","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fair. Let me lay out the safer wins more concretely.\n\n**B-lite — parallelize compute-only work (recommended):**\n\nThe risk in \"full B\" is putting concurrent writers on the go-git store. We can sidestep that entirely:\n\n- Worker pool does **pure CPU work**: `compact.Compact`, `agent.ChunkTranscript`, sha256, prompt joining. They produce blob *bytes* in memory.\n- Main goroutine does **all I/O serially**: reads v1 transcripts, hands work to workers, collects results in input order, calls `CreateBlobFromContent` and the v2 ref CAS.\n\nSo the per-session sequence becomes: main reads v1 (16ms) → enqueue → worker compacts+chunks+hashes (~50ms CPU) → main writes blobs+ref (~20ms). With workers running concurrently and the main thread mostly waiting on I/O, the 2m of compact + roughly half the 2m of pack collapses toward `compact_time / num_cores`.\n\n- **Win estimate:** ~-2m (5m38s → ~3m30s) on an 8-core machine; ~-1m on a 4-core\n- **Risk:** ordering bugs (coordinator collects via sequenced channel — easy to test) and memory pressure if we let too many transcripts queue up (cap with a bounded channel)\n- **No go-git thread-safety concerns** because the storer only sees one goroutine\n\n**C — batch /main writes per generation (~ -30-40s):**\n\nToday there are ~2478 individual `refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/main` CAS updates, each rebuilding the root tree. Migration knows session indexes deterministically from v1 (we don't need to read /main to resolve them), so we can:\n- Buffer all per-session /main entries during a `batchSize` window\n- Do **one** /main commit per batch alongside the existing /full archive\n\nGoes from ~2478 ref updates to ~3. Lowers the 51s `write_v2_session` stage to maybe 5-10s.\n- **Risk:** small — deterministic session-index assignment, mid-migration crashes are already idempotent via `fullArtifactsIndex`\n- **Independent of B-lite** — they compose\n\n**My recommendation:** start with B-lite. It's the bigger win, the risks are bug-shaped (testable) rather than semantic (hard to characterize), and we can layer C on top later.\n\nWant me to implement B-lite?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2511,"cache_read_input_tokens":112415,"output_tokens":6509,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2511,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":6509,"cache_read_input_tokens":112415,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2511,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2511},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaojHqBDBhJFuDbWWDBjv","type":"assistant","uuid":"cde0fe89-c47b-4b1b-84f2-8e94fd15c670","timestamp":"2026-05-07T19:06:52.711Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/ninawork/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"2258e038-9f02-499e-98ec-73c37394ea23","version":"2.1.132","gitBranch":"migration-performance-improvements"}
